tasks.description:
TDD. Add `runPostTaskReview()` to `src/post-task-reviewer.ts`.

Interface:
```ts
interface RunPostTaskReviewOpts {
  projectRoot: string;
  dataDir: string;
  task: Task;
  taskStatus: string;
  beforeSha: string | null;
  config: RalphConfig;
  streamOpts?: ProcessStreamOptions;
  deps?: {
    captureGitSha?: typeof captureGitSha;
    getGitDiff?: typeof getGitDiff;
    spawnPostTaskReviewer?: typeof spawnPostTaskReviewer;
    log?: (...args: any[]) => void;
  };
}
```

Skip conditions (return early, log reason):
1. `config.review?.postTask` is not true
2. `taskStatus` is not 'complete'
3. `beforeSha` is null
4. Current SHA equals beforeSha (no commits made) — call `deps.captureGitSha(projectRoot)`

Happy path: call `deps.getGitDiff(projectRoot, beforeSha)`, then `deps.spawnPostTaskReviewer()` with task + diff data. Log start/completion. Return void (informational, never throws).

Wrap the entire function body in try/catch — log errors but never throw (review must not break the run loop).

Tests cover: each skip condition returns early without spawning, happy path calls getGitDiff and spawnPostTaskReviewer with correct args, errors are caught and logged.
